35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the firms say the clay is risky, but shallow work is fine. The depot notes say we can keep the south open. Does that help your drainage worries?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the clay is a risk, but the data is worse. Callouts doubled, and heat is spiking. People stick to firm ground, ignoring the margins.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I found the roll is down to seven, but two volunteer groups help weekends. Does that cover the daily care?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the basin survived, but the apron failed. The avenue trees died from neglect. We must judge by what actually lasts, not the drawings.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the ledger shows planted ground costs triple to maintain. The fund only pays for planting, not surfacing. We must price that gap now.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, the avenue trees died because aftercare was missing. If we pick a plan needing constant care, we must ensure the contract includes it, or it will fail too.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, the basin surviving while the apron failed is telling. But my data shows people ignore soft margins. We need a plan that respects both the water and the foot traffic.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, that is worrying. With only seven staff, can the volunteers really handle the daily work?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the basin survived because it was simple. The apron failed because it was complex. We must choose a plan that is robust enough to survive our current staffing levels.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, simplicity is wise, but the ledger is unforgiving. Planted ground costs triple to maintain. We must ensure the plan fits our shrinking budget, not just our ideals.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the firms say shallow work is safe. If we keep the south open, we avoid the worst clay risks. Does that ease your mind about the digging?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the digging is manageable, but the heat and drainage data are alarming. We need a plan that cools the site and handles the water, not just one that is easy to dig.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I worry the volunteers can’t handle heavy water work. The casual pool helps weekends, but who manages the daily upkeep with only seven staff?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the basin survived because it was simple. The apron failed because it was complex. We must choose a plan that is robust enough to survive our current staffing levels.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, the ledger confirms your fear. Planted ground costs triple to maintain. With only seven staff, we cannot afford the upkeep. We must choose a plan that is cheap to keep alive.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the heat and drainage are serious. But if we pick a plan needing deep digging, the clay risk is real. We need something simple that works with the ground, not against it.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, agreed. The data shows people need firm ground, but the heat and drainage are critical. We need a plan that cools the site and manages water, without demanding impossible upkeep.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I agree. With only seven staff, we need a plan that is simple to maintain. The volunteers help, but they cannot do everything.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The basin survived because it was simple. The apron failed because it was complex. We must choose a plan that is robust enough to survive our current staffing levels.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The fund covers planting, not surfacing. If we choose water features, the city pays triple for upkeep. We must pick what we can actually afford to maintain.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
